      "message": "Actually, apparently it wasn\u0027t ready. Not sure how I missed the failing test. Uploaded a new patch. The change is in inspector_test.cc line 598. I\u0027m not actually sure that test should stay as is. It creates a fragment entrypoint function with 3 variables. Two of them have a location and Flat interpolation. One of them has neither a location nor any interpolation. That to me seems like an error. AFAIK there is no automatic location. There used to be a tint rule that an inter-stage variable of type u32 or i32 would automatically get flat interpolation but that rule is removed in this CL and they get perspective by default. That also seems like an error condition (int value with perspective interpolation). So should I just remove \"in_var4\", and, is it passing when it shouldn\u0027t?",
